# Enforce LF line endings for every text file on all platforms.
#
# Without this, the Windows CI runner (git's default `core.autocrlf=true`) checks out
# text files with CRLF, and oxfmt — which `vp check` / `vp fmt` run and which enforces
# LF — then flags every file as mis-formatted (the `test (windows-latest)` job). Every
# committed blob is already LF, so this only changes checkout behavior on Windows; it
# triggers no renormalization of existing files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never apply any line-ending conversion.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.avif  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.wasm  binary
*.mp4   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
